    "result_text": "Full suite is green \u2014 **68 tests, 0 failures**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the read-only `ownerSegment` field on the owner read model (`GET /api/owners/{id}`), formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` schema property (read-only enum: `PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), which the OpenAPI generator turns into `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/common/OwnerSegments.java`** (new) \u2014 a small derivation helper matching the existing `AgeBands`/`Localities` style:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevels.of(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - AREA = `METRO` when `Localities.region(postcode, city)` resolves to a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL` (i.e. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", \u2026)` expression wiring the helper into the DTO mapping, alongside the other derived fields.\n\nThis reuses the existing `MembershipLevels` and `Localities` logic rather than reimplementing tier/region rules, so the segment stays consistent with the `membershipLevel` and `locality` fields already exposed.",
